# The repository stores LF, and Biome's formatter expects LF. Without this file a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF on the way out, and `pnpm lint`
# then fails on files nobody edited — a whole-file "needs formatting" diff with no
# visible change in it. Pin the working-tree ending instead of relying on each
# machine's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.db binary

# Lockfiles are generated: keep them out of diffs and merges by hand.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated

# Impeccable, vendored (docs/agents/impeccable.md). cmd.exe parses a batch file by byte offset, so an
# LF-only `.cmd` breaks its `call :label` and `goto`: the Windows launcher keeps CRLF, as upstream's
# own .gitattributes pins it. The tree is upstream's build output, so it is collapsed in PR diffs.
.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable.cmd text eol=crlf
.claude/skills/impeccable/** linguist-generated
.claude/agents/impeccable-*.md linguist-generated
